              "inline_data": null,
              "text": "To log into your Wells Fargo credit card account, you can access your online portal through the options below, depending on the type of card you have:\n\n### 1. For Standard Wells Fargo Credit Cards \n*(e.g., Wells Fargo Active Cash\u00ae, Autograph\u2120, Reflect\u00ae, etc.)*\n* **Official Website:** Go directly to the **[Wells Fargo Home Page](https://www.wellsfargo.com)**. \n* **How to Log In:** On the homepage, locate the **Sign On** box, enter your Username and Password, and click **Sign On**.\n* **Alternative Direct Link:** You can also go straight to the **[Wells Fargo Online Sign On](https://www.wellsfargo.com)** portal.\n\n### 2. For Retail / Partner Store Credit Cards \n*(e.g., cards issued by Wells Fargo for specific furniture, jewelry, or home improvement stores)*\n* **Official Website:** If your card was issued through a retail store partner, you will need to log in through the **[Wells Fargo Retail Services Portal](https://retailservices.wellsfargo.com)**. \n* **How to Log In:** Click the **Sign On** button on that page to manage your store card payments and statement history.\n\n### 3. Log In via the Mobile App\nIf you prefer managing your credit card on your phone:\n* Download the official **Wells Fargo Mobile\u00ae app** from the Apple App Store or Google Play Store. \n* Logging in through the app allows you to use secure biometric login (Face ID/Fingerprint), pay your bill, view your transactions, and set up card alerts.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udd12 Security Tips for Logging In safely:\n* **Verify the URL:** Always make sure the website address begins with `https://www.wellsfargo.com/` or `https://retailservices.wellsfargo.com/` before entering your credentials. Look for the lock icon in your browser's address bar.\n* **Avoid Search Ad Links:** Sometimes scam artists buy search ads that mimic bank login screens. Avoid clicking on links labeled \"Ad\" or \"Sponsored\" on search engines; instead, type the URL directly into your address bar.\n* **Never Share Codes:** Wells Fargo will never call, text, or email you asking for your password or one-time access verification codes.",
